      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing on specific guest \"profiles\" based on behavior rather than demographics is the best approach to update your SOPs while avoiding discrimination and maintaining a welcoming environment. Instead of labeling certain groups as higher risk, your new policy should prioritize observing specific disruptive patterns, such as repeated partying, loud music late at night, or guests ignoring stay-inizierte quiet hours. Staff should be trained to address these behaviors calmly and consistently by offering privacy solutions or ampenable with escalating to security only when all direct resolves fail. This proactive, behavior-focused strategy helps protect the peace without stigmatizing any particular type of traveler.",
